# fuzz.bc.1 (seed 1585 minimised): `xs[3].step(ARG)` with ARG that traps. The walker traps on the index first (type.coll.4), the tier on ARG (expr.arith.1). The walker is the oracle: a receiver is evaluated before its arguments.
struct Acc
    a int

fn Acc.step(mut self, d int)
    self.a += d

fn main()
    mut xs := [Acc(a: 1)]
    for i in 0..1
        xs[3].step(4611686018427387904 * 3037000500)
